> [3]: While standing on or in water, dipping (or perhaps engraving with)
> a wand of lightning should have the effect of electrocuting nearby
> monsters (and possibly you). --aioli

Perhaps zapping or engraving with the wand while in water should have
the same effect as breaking it (except for destroying the wand)?

> [4]: The Book should be readable in Braille to simplify the description
> (and future official implementation) of the zen conduct. --aioli

Silly, but harmless enough.  "You carefully feel the lettering with
your fingers..."?  Presumably it should not work while wearing gloves.

> [5]: There should be a #call command, to avoid the need for a prompt in
> #name. --SimonRC

Yes, that'd be useful.  There is already the (C)all command, though.
Still, if we can have both (z)ap and (Z)ap..

> [6]: There should be a chance of catching a thrown potion based on
> dexterity. This chance could never excede 50% though to account for
> potions thrown at you from behind.  One would never be able to catch a
> potion thrown by an unseen monster.  --azgor

Shouldn't that require having at least one hand free?  I just can't
visualize anyone catching a thrown bottle while wearing a shield on
one hand and wielding a drawn sword in the other.  Of course, if
you're not engaged in melee right now, your sword is presumably in its
scabbard... hmm...

> [7]: There should be a command called "pour" which allows you to dump
> out a potion and keep the empty bottle. Might also be used for ID
> purposes? --Dragonmaw

As someone already noted, nethack has no empty bottles.  More to the
point, adding empty bottles would require some significant changes to
other parts of the game to avoid unbalancing things.

(In particular, having a quaffed potion leave an empty bottle, which
could then presumably be refilled with water, would make potions of
water a practically limitless resource, and would thus make blessing
things too easy unless the conversion of water to holy water was
somehow made more difficult.)

> [10]: Wading: Large enough creatures should be able to just walk into
> pools and use them, much like creatures with the ability to swim.
> --TheShrewdDude

Don't they already do that?  Or maybe I'm just mistaken...

> [12]: Valkyries should start with a tame wolf and they should be able
> to ride wolves as per Norse mythology.

The riding wolves part seems a nice enough touch (but of course you'll
have to tame it first, and no, a tripe ration won't do it).

If they were to start with a tame one, it'd presumably have to be a
wolf *pup*.

> [15]: If prayer uncurses a worn blindfold, it should produce a message
> to show that it was uncursed. --NESoutlaw_

"Your <blindfold> loosens a little."?

